      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should r6-r9 be reallocated to the call-clobbered range of r16-r19?  That way they wouldn\u0027t need to be saved and restored by __mulsf3.  You could also set __mulsf3 to be an alias of __mulsf3_div_div.\n\n\nRef: AndeStar Instruction Set Architecture Manual, sec 1.4, table 1 describes r6-r14 as callee-saved, and r16-r25 as call-clobbered.  Is GCC complying with this procedure call standard, or is it using another one?",
